WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.758
Here's the box.

00:00:01.758 --> 00:00:09.980
Each corner has an angle: sixty by fifty by ten on the left, fifty by forty by eight on the right.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:17.271
An angle's area is the sum of its legs minus the overlap, times thickness.

00:00:17.271 --> 00:00:19.859
Left: one thousand square millimeters.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:21.833
Right: six hundred fifty six.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:26.708
The top and bottom skins have the same stress at both ends, ratio one.

00:00:26.708 --> 00:00:31.607
Each gives ten times five hundred over two: twenty five hundred to each corner.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:39.300
The webs cross the neutral axis, ratio minus one: five hundred from the left web, four hundred from the right.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:48.019
The box is symmetric about its horizontal axis, so I x y is zero.

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:58.460
I x x is two times four thousand plus three thousand five hundred fifty six, times one fifty squared.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.862
Put a vertical load S y somewhere, at a distance xi from the left web.

00:01:06.862 --> 00:01:11.860
Cut the top wall, and go around: one, two, three, four.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.134
Wall one two: zero.

00:01:14.134 --> 00:01:21.356
Crossing boom two: minus S y over I x x, times three five five six, times one fifty.

00:01:21.356 --> 00:01:27.460
That's minus one point five six nine times ten to the minus three, S y.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.453
Boom three is at minus one fifty, so it cancels that: wall three four is zero.

00:01:33.453 --> 00:01:40.120
Boom four brings the left web to plus one point seven six five times ten to the minus three.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.426
At the shear center the box doesn't twist.

00:01:44.426 --> 00:01:50.853
With one material, that means the integral of q d s over t around the box is zero.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:02:01.535
d s over t for each wall: fifty on top, thirty seven and a half on the right, fifty on the bottom, thirty on the left.

00:02:01.535 --> 00:02:05.413
One hundred sixty seven and a half in total.

00:02:05.766 --> 00:02:08.035
Only the two webs have basic flow.

00:02:08.035 --> 00:02:18.646
Minus one point five six nine times thirty seven and a half, plus one point seven six five times thirty, plus one sixty seven and a half q s zero, equals zero.

00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:25.833
So q s zero is three point five two times ten to the minus five, S y.

00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:29.733
A small correction, all the way around.

00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:33.925
Both webs now carry shear flow upward.

00:02:33.925 --> 00:02:42.101
Times three hundred millimeters, the right web carries zero point four six S y, the left web zero point five four.

00:02:42.101 --> 00:02:43.679
Together, exactly S y.

00:02:44.066 --> 00:02:46.599
Take moments about the left web.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:55.066
The right web's force, zero point four six S y, acts five hundred millimeters away: two hundred thirty S y.

00:02:55.466 --> 00:03:02.106
The small flows in the top and bottom skins form a couple the other way, about five point three S y.

00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:12.869
So S y times xi equals two thirty minus five point three, and xi is two hundred twenty four point eight millimeters from the left web.

00:03:12.869 --> 00:03:17.152
Left of the middle, because the left booms are heavier.

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:18.163
Your turn.

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:23.332
Pause here and do checkpoint three point one: the same steps for the practice box.
